# /sdlc-verify

Run `./scripts/sdlc verify` (on Windows PowerShell or cmd: `.\scripts\sdlc.cmd verify`). It is exactly what CI runs: all gates, then the checks in each feature's
`acceptance.json` against the **running** system. That starts the whole stack and can take minutes: give the command up to 10 minutes (or run it in the background and wait for it).

Then read `.ai/evidence/latest/report.md` and tell the person:

- the verdict (PASSED or FAILED) and the run id;
- the gates that failed, if any;
- for each feature, a table of its acceptance criteria (AC-001, ...) with PASS, FAIL or SKIP, and the check ids behind each.

If it could not start the system at all (for example Docker is not running), say exactly that, tell the person to start Docker (or to change `runtime.mode` in `.ai/sdlc.json`), and stop.
Green: say so and stop. Red: for each failure say what the check expected, what it got, and where the log is, and your best explanation of the cause.
**This command only reports.** Do not change any file, the spec or the code: if the person wants a failure fixed they will say so (and for a whole feature,
`/sdlc-implement FEAT-001` builds and heals it). A check shown as SKIP was not run: say why it says it was skipped, and never count it as a pass.
